From c661c2843362b441973b411af3f6cd8b765ada30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XAScraft refactor <refactor@xascraft.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Temporary: path2chi and _calc_chi use path parameters given
 as keywords

Upstream c18a4ed63 ("move hashkey to FeffDatFile, several cleanups")
added an "if parname in self.params" check to FeffPathGroup.__path_params
and indented out.append(val) under it. A path parameter given as a
keyword then never reaches the list, so _calc_chi unpacks fewer than its
seven values: path2chi(path, sigma2=0.005) and
_calc_chi(k=k, sigma2=0.005) raise "not enough values to unpack
(expected 7, got 6)". At 8d6cd41c2 the keyword's value was used in place
of the path's own.

This moves out.append(val) back to the loop, as at 8d6cd41c2, and
nothing else. Upstream's check stays: a path parameter that is neither
given nor in the path's Parameters now gives None instead of being left
out (at 8d6cd41c2 it raised KeyError).

Remove once upstream fixes this (exit condition in larch-patches/README.md).
---
 larch/xafs/feffdat.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/larch/xafs/feffdat.py b/larch/xafs/feffdat.py
index a5d54cf2e358b29cb8abd2bf3b81e81787f307df..4c2ff6bd513ce3104137b0c6060918f4b9de188b 100644
--- a/larch/xafs/feffdat.py
+++ b/larch/xafs/feffdat.py
@@ -580,7 +580,7 @@ class FeffPathGroup(Group):
                 parname = self.pathpar_name(pname)
                 if parname in self.params:
                     val = self.params[parname]._getval()
-                    out.append(val)
+            out.append(val)
         return out
 
     def path_paramvals(self, **kws):
